4.2
GRACE as a universal refiner
Table 1 reports DSC and HD95 on real upstream segmentor outputs; Fig. 3 summarises the evaluation under
the three synthetic corruption severities. GRACE-M yields the largest DSC lift in three of the five upstream
settings, with GRACE-U ahead on U-Net@30 and U-Net@150, and the three GRACE variants provide the
three strongest HD95 reductions in every setting. Appendix D gives how often refinement decreases the DSC
for each band of input DSC.
The benefit of retrieval grows monotonically with corruption severity, and GRACE-U and GRACE-M reduce
HD95 at every severity while retrieval-free refiners are less stable (PostDAE and U-Net w/o RAG both
degrade under stronger corruption).
The same pattern holds for real upstream segmentors in Table 1:
strong-tier mean changes remain non-negative for all three variants and are much smaller than the weak-tier
gains.
