updated. We call this protocol held-out dataset transfer. The anatomies and modalities of these datasets also
occur in other training datasets. Thus, the protocol measures transfer under dataset and acquisition shift,
and it is not a zero-shot evaluation. Sec. 4.4 removes a full modality. When verified target-dataset masks are
inserted into K instead, the protocol becomes a parameter-free index extension as in Sec. 4.4. Table 2 reports
