Transfer to a held-out anatomy or modality
The held-out datasets of Sec. 4.3 have anatomies and modalities that also occur in the training corpus. This
subsection removes a full anatomy or a full imaging modality. In both experiments, we remove the held-out
data from the training data and from the retrieval index. Then we retrain the refiner from scratch. Table 3
gives the results.
Held-out anatomy.
We evaluate whether GRACE can refine a previously unseen anatomical class without
updating its parameters. For each anatomy a in {Liver, Spleen, Pancreas, Prostate PZ}, we retrain the refiner
without a. At test time, we add verified support cases of a to K. Thus, the experiment is a parameter-free
index extension. The refiner receives no gradient from a, but the index gives it examples of a. The support
cases are disjoint from the evaluation queries. Both variants improve every held-out anatomy, with mean
