3.4.4. Boundary Regularization and Training Objective
A gated conditional random field (CRF) loss, LCRF ,
grounds the predicted boundaries in the underlying image
appearance. Pixels that are spatially close and similar in intensity are encouraged to receive the same label, while disagreement across an intensity edge is left unpenalized. This
supplies complementary supervision in the unlabeled region
between the foreground and background strokes. The complete objective combines the four terms
L = λpCELpCE +λconsLcons +λtempLtemp +λCRFLCRF
