Qualitative comparison. Figure 5 presents qualitative
comparisons between FGCARL and Lifelong-nnUNet on
both the original and incrementally adapted domains. In the
previously learned domain, FGCARL preserved the overall
morphology and spatial localization of the metastatic lesions
after adaptation to the new domain. In contrast, LifelongnnUNet exhibit more pronounced prediction errors, including incomplete lesion delineation, spurious predictions, and
