by far the largest training set, and two of its three test sets originate from the same archive as
the training data, representing a milder shift. PH2, the one genuinely independent skin source,
shows the smallest deficit of the three under the plain U-Net, which does not support the second
explanation. Section 4.4 addresses the first.
The other metrics agree with DSC out of distribution except at the finest scale of the
boundary. DINOv2 is best on all eight out-of-distribution sets in IoU, sensitivity and HD95,
and on seven in precision and ASSD; the exceptions are precision on ISIC 2016*, and ASSD on
CVC-ColonDB, where the maximum distance assigned to its empty predictions (Section 4.3)
outweighs its advantage on the remaining images. NSD at the 2/224 tolerance does not follow:
a task-specific model leads on four of the eight sets, all four evaluated at 224 pixels, and in
