We propose DeVAR (Fig. 1), a novel generative framework adapting visual
autoregressive modeling (VAR) for low-dose CT (LDCT) denoising. Given an
input LDCT image, a pyramid-style encoder extracts LDCT prefix tokens
rLDCT , which provide global contextual guidance to an autoregressive transformer
predicting the discrete token maps of the target normal-dose CT (NDCT). To
recover high-frequency anatomical details inherently lost during quantization, a
lightweight diffusion-based residual refiner estimates the residual discrepancy
ˆf ′ between the continuous and discrete latents. Finally, a hybrid NDCT decoder
