E. Simulation Methodology
The simulation evaluates system performance under varying
ECG data rates (16–256 kbps) to assess how the system
behaves under increasing load. The methodology begins with
the network setup, where a topology is built, IP addresses are
assigned, and routing (OLSR) is installed. For mobility, the
patient nodes are assigned using the RandomWalk2d model
within defined bounds to simulate realistic movement. Applications are configured by using OnOff applications for sensors
with DSCP marking, with a VoiceReminder being sent from
the CommHub to the patients and an email being sent from
the CommHub to the medical center. To ensure quality of service, FQ-CoDel is implemented on the CommHub→Satellite
link. Finally, monitoring is enabled through FlowMonitor
and NetAnim to provide detailed analysis of the network’s
performance after the simulation.
