C. Packet Delivery Ratio (PDR)
Fig 5 shows the PDR for each traffic class. At low transmission rates (16–64 kbps), all classes maintain a near-perfect
PDR (>99%). As the rate increases, BE traffic drops sharply
to 55% at 256 kbps due to buffer overflow and packet drops,
as BE packets are discarded first. EF traffic maintains an
