B. Primary Model Performance (60-Second Recordings)
The primary SoNUS model, optimized for 60-second
recordings, achieved improved performance due to
increased temporal context and stronger consistency
checks. Across all annotated recordings (n = 38), the
mean HR error was 8.37%, corresponding to a mean
HR accuracy of 91.63%. The median HR error was
5.05%, yielding a median HR accuracy of 94.95%.
When filtering by quality score, 32 out of 38 recordings (84.21%) had a QS ≥70 and were deemed suitable
for result presentation within the application.
