Within this framework, b(a | s) represents the behavior model,
which characterizes the likelihood that a human expert would
select action a from the total set of possible interventions A
for a patient in state s. The support threshold, τsupp, acts as a
safety gate to exclude actions that lack sufficient evidence in
historical clinical data, ensuring the model avoids unproven or
potentially hazardous decisions. This threshold is tuned during
validation to effectively balance the optimization of treatment
outcomes with rigorous safety requirements.
