(1)
where r denotes spatial locations and t time. Cm denotes membrane capacitance, χ is the membrane surface-to-volume ratio, D is the conductivity (or
diffusion) tensor, Iion is the total ionic current, Iapp is an externally applied
stimulus current, and w collects additional recovery, gating, and concentration variables [9, 31, 12].
This formulation highlights the two core ingredients shared by a broad
family of EP models. The diffusion term, ∇· (D∇u), governs the spatial
spread of excitation through electrically coupled tissue. It depends on physiological properties that govern intercellular electrical coupling, including myocardial fiber organization, anisotropic tissue conductivity, and structural
heterogeneity which are difficult to measure and thus associated with significant uncertainties in personalized modeling. The reaction terms, represented
by Iion(u, w) together with the state dynamics F(u, w), govern the local nonlinear membrane kinetics underlying depolarization, recovery, and refractoriness [9, 31]. Many models under the monodomain family differ primarily
