to specific measurements from a specific instance, known interchangeably as
personalization, calibration, or adaptation in different works. These apply to
the optimization of most mechanistic and PINN models [14, 6, 17, 16, 50],
while some recent works also considered per-instance optimization of the input mechanistic parameters θ to a black-box neural surrogate Mϕ(θ) to fit
observed patient-specific data [29, 38].
This per-instance inference can be generally expressed as:
