objective where the hybrid DT is asked to use the latent parameters zPHY and
zNN, inferred from context samples Dc, to predict for query examples xq that
are different from Dc. This is fundamentally different from reconstructionbased objectives.
Interestingly, optimizing the ELBO in (13) corresponds to a feedforward
meta-learning process performed over tasks defined by individual patients or
patient-subgroups, depending on the problem of interest. Given data from
multiple such tasks, the conditioning on Dc realized via Equations (10)-(11)
work as meta-models that provide inner-loop task adaptation, and the expected query log-likelihood defines the outer-loop meta-objective for optimizing the meta-models. Notably, unlike gradient-based meta-learning (e.g.,
