Self-Evolving RAG Knowledge Bases
S4.1
Doctor Experience Rules Base (3,085 Rules)
Over the iterative training loop on 14, 000 training stays, the
reflection agent accumulated 3,085 rules:
• Mortality Rules (N = 2, 951): Rules differentiating
acute reversible organ decompensation from catastrophic
multi-system failure.
• Readmission Rules (N = 2, 773): Rules capturing premature discharge under ward saturation, incomplete diuretic titration, post-extubation subglottic stridor, and
telemetry instability.
Table S3 provides representative rules categorized across 7
core physiological domains.
S4.2
Golden Case Base (1,899 Cases) and Case
Walkthrough
A clinical stay is archived into case_base.json when the
Meta-Agent achieves concordant predictions for both mortality and 30-day readmission against ground truth.
End-to-End Case Walkthrough (Stay ID: 232669)
• Demographics: 68-year-old male, emergency CCU admission, 3 pre-ICU transfers.
• Ground Truth: In-hospital Mortality = 1 (Deceased),
30-day Readmission = 0 (Mutual exclusion).
• Raw Domain Summaries:
– Nursing/other: “Agitated, receiving Dexmedetomidine
infusion. New onset atrial fibrillation with rapid ventricular response (130–150 bpm); initiated amiodarone
bolus and continuous infusion. Neurological status
fluctuating from confused to obtunded.”
– ECG Summary: “Atrial fibrillation with rapid ventricular response. ST segment depression in leads V4–V6.
Non-specific intraventricular conduction delay.”
• Retrieved RAG Rules:
– Rule 1: [Mortality Rule]: If acute severe neurological deterioration coexists with refractory tachyarrhythmias, prioritize mortality risk.
– Rule 2: [Readmission Rule]: Rate readmission risk
moderate if patient remains on active continuous antiarrhythmic infusions.
