S7.3
Temporal Cross-Attention Dynamics
Transformer self-attention between the [CLS] token and
the 48 hourly vital sign vectors partitions into three clinically meaningful phases: (1) Acute Resuscitation Phase
(Hours 0–12): 37.9% of total attention, reflecting initial
resuscitation response, drug loading, and mechanical ventilation establishment; (2) Continuous Monitoring Phase
(Hours 12–36): 42.3%, capturing intermediate clinical stability and multi-organ recovery; and (3) Pre-Discharge Tapering Phase (Hours 36–48): 19.7%, evaluating extubation
tolerance, pressor weaning, and ward readiness. Table S8
provides the Top-10 most attended individual hours.
